### ============================================
### LEVEL 3 (HATEOAS) API Test Requests
### ============================================
### Use with REST Client extension in VS Code
### ============================================

### ============================================
### 1. API DISCOVERY ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 1.1 API Root - Entry Point for Discovery
GET http://localhost:5000/

### 1.2 API Documentation
GET http://localhost:5000/docs

### 1.3 Health Check
GET http://localhost:5000/health

### ============================================
### 2. HATEOAS - FOLLOWING LINKS
### ============================================

### 2.1 Get All Tasks (with links)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/tasks

### 2.2 Get Single Task (with links)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/tasks/1

### 2.3 Get Non-existent Task (404 with links)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/tasks/999

### ============================================
### 3. CREATE TASK (follow link from collection)
### ============================================

### 3.1 Create New Task
POST http://localhost:5000/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learn HATEOAS",
  "description": "Understand hypermedia-driven APIs"
}

### 3.2 Create Task - Missing Title (400 Error)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "This should fail because title is missing"
}

### ============================================
### 4. UPDATE TASK (follow update link)
### ============================================

### 4.1 Mark Task as Complete (use mark_complete link)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "completed": true
}

### 4.2 Update Task Title and Description
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tasks/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated: Build Task API",
  "description": "Create REST endpoints with HATEOAS links"
}

### 4.3 Mark Task as Incomplete (use mark_incomplete link)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "completed": false
}

### 4.4 Update Non-existent Task (404 with links)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tasks/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "This task does not exist"
}

### ============================================
### 5. DELETE TASK (follow delete link)
### ============================================

### 5.1 Delete Task
DELETE http://localhost:5000/api/tasks/3

### 5.2 Delete Non-existent Task (404 with links)
DELETE http://localhost:5000/api/tasks/999

### ============================================
### 6. ERROR HANDLING (responses with links)
### ============================================

### 6.1 Invalid Route (404 with HATEOAS links)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/invalid-endpoint

### 6.2 Invalid JSON (400 Bad Request)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  invalid json here
}

### ============================================
### 7. COMPLETE WORKFLOW EXAMPLE
### ============================================
### This demonstrates full HATEOAS navigation

### Step 1: Start at API Root
GET http://localhost:5000/

### Step 2: Follow 'tasks' link to get all tasks
GET http://localhost:5000/api/tasks

### Step 3: Extract task._links.update and update task
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated via HATEOAS link",
  "completed": true
}

### Step 4: Follow collection link to see all tasks
GET http://localhost:5000/api/tasks

### Step 5: Follow create link to add new task
POST http://localhost:5000/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "New Task from HATEOAS Link",
  "description": "Created by following the create link"
}

### Step 6: Follow api-root link to go back home
GET http://localhost:5000/

### ============================================
### NOTES:
### ============================================
### 
### 1. Each response includes _links object
### 2. Use link.href and link.method to navigate
### 3. Link titles explain what each action does
### 4. Some links include 'body' with suggested payload
### 5. Clients can discover API without hardcoding URLs
### 6. Error responses also include helpful links
### 7. This is Richardson Maturity Model Level 3 (HATEOAS)
###
### ============================================
